// 2026-11-15 (landing 177d2b7, row 1: DEF-660's K-a2 as V1 with F6). THE RIGHT CONTROLS OF `header_store_target.npk`: each `nw_` cell stores the caller's
// own `@k`, which outlives every read, through a local's or a by-value parameter's buffer, string or cstring header (the address spelling's two keep the
// header's first word and write it back before the header drops); each `nt_` cell is `lib/ntensor.npk`'s store through a header reached through `self`
// (`self.cells.ptr =>! wild T->` in a method and a free function, a string's and a cstring's `.ptr`, a ternary of two casts, a value handed to a storing
// callee, and `int64` stores with no `#ptr_add`), which a record on `self`'s own chain refused beside the cast's `@self` party (`nt_vb_ok` before F6, and the
// rest with row 2's rootless destination). Each runs its exit on main (78f9b3a) and with this row, at -O0 and -O2 and under the freed-heap detector.
// One cell a case, its names suffixed with the cell's; `main` exits with the case's number when a case returns other than its exit on main.
